# NestFlow TypeScript Conventions

- Place imports at the top of the file. No inline imports unless a documented circular-dependency exception exists.
- Prefer Server Components by default. Mark Client Components with `"use client"` only when required.
- Validate all external input with Zod.
- Use exhaustive `switch` handling for unions and enums, with a `never` check in the default case.
- Colocate feature logic under clear domain folders. Prefer shared UI from NestFlow components built on shadcn/ui.
- Do not use `any`. Prefer unknown + narrowing.
- Server Actions and Route Handlers must enforce authentication and authorisation before mutating data.
- Keep UI copy free of em dashes used as stylistic pauses (see dash-usage rule).
